<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gangotri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gangotri is a town and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> pilgrimage site in the Uttarkashi district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttarakhand">Uttarakhand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, high in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalaya</a> on the Bhagirathi, the headstream of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>. Its temple to the goddess Ganga is one of the four sites of the Char Dham pilgrimage, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamunotri">Yamunotri</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kedarnath">Kedarnath</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badrinath">Badrinath</a>. The Gangotri Glacier, the river's source, lies upstream at Gaumukh.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gangotri.jpg" alt="Gangotri" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dhwani Shree · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gangotri_(ganga_river).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
